+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are ignored unless the `-l` /
+`--links` flag is in use. With `--links` a symlink is listed under its
+name plus a `.rclonelink` suffix, its size is the length of the target
+and reading it returns the target path. Copying with `--links` to a
+destination which supports symlinks recreates them.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+An archive member whose name happens to end in `.rclonelink` is
+treated as an ordinary file, not a symlink.
+
 ## Modification times
 
 Modification times are preserved with an accuracy depending on the archive type.
